Dear Kellan,

Thank you for your call from 16 Brindlewick Mews. The landlord has confirmed that her authority covers only the quoted plumbing work, not a specialist assessment of the lining. She has asked for the likely cost and timing before she considers anything further.

Please send us:
- the likely cost and earliest timing for identifying the pale, fibrous-looking lining behind the kitchen ceiling board, or, if you do not do this, the type of specialist you would recommend and any indication of their cost and lead time;
- whether the plumbing work could be done without disturbing the lining, and if not, what would change in your scope and price;
- your complete all-inclusive total for the quoted plumbing work, stating whether VAT is included, and whether making good is included.

Please do not drill, cut, open the ceiling, touch the lining or start any work. Nothing is approved beyond the quoted plumbing scope. We will pass your answer to the landlord and tell you her decision.

Kind regards,
Northbridge Lettings
